# taskforge-web/src/main.sem — EAV port (apps/taskforge-web, semsc v0.1).
#
# The 18-operation sqlite/bcrypt/json/session API module: lifecycle
# (openOrReuseDatabase), JSON response helpers, session resolution, and the
# health/version/register/login/logout/me + todo-CRUD handlers, plus the
# webServer entity routing them. Converted from the v0.1 module to EAV against
# sigs/standard.{http,sqlite,json,bcrypt,log}.semsig (§20 call split). Execution
# is deferred (target webServer); the project lives in build.sem (§28.2).
#
# Conversions: bind ok/value -> call `out`; bind error + branch error source ->
# `catch` + `branch ifError ... goto`; ignore -> discards; storage module ->
# single-line storage; literal+literalSource -> storage+literalSource; sql body/
# jsonBody -> storage body islands; useCapability -> uses; authority dropped;
# capability NAME EFFECT ACCESS -> grants ACCESS EFFECT; set storage -> set;
# resource defers -> cleanup entities (owns/cleanedBy); transaction-rollback
# action defers dropped (EAV defer is handle-scoped).

appTaskforgeWeb is module
appTaskforgeWeb path apps.taskforgeWeb
appTaskforgeWeb imports http standard.http
appTaskforgeWeb imports sqlite standard.sqlite
appTaskforgeWeb imports json standard.json
appTaskforgeWeb imports bcrypt standard.bcrypt
appTaskforgeWeb imports html standard.html
appTaskforgeWeb imports log standard.log
appTaskforgeWeb imports pages app.taskforge_web.pages
appTaskforgeWeb exports taskForgeWebServer
appTaskforgeWeb purpose "Multi-user todo web API: bcrypt auth, SQLite-backed per-user data, JSON REST"
appTaskforgeWeb invariant "Every authed /api route resolves the session user id before any SQL and scopes every query by user_id"

