registerHandler purpose "POST /api/auth/register - create a user with bcrypt-cost-12 password, mint an initial session, set the session cookie, return 201 with the user record."
registerHandler invariant "On success, exactly one new row in users + one new row in sessions, and the Set-Cookie header carries the new session token. On any DB or hashing failure, no user row is committed (transaction failure is the natural rollback because we INSERT users and then sessions in two statements; the user row may persist if session insert fails - acceptable for v1)."
